{
  "info": {
    "name": "Grievance Dashboard Service",
    "description": "Aggregate chart data for the OAN programme dashboards: GET /api/v1/charts/{chart_id}.\n\nPublic: no Authorization header is sent. Rows are counts only, never a ticket number, a title, a submitter or any grievance text. Data comes from rollup tables the scheduler rebuilds every 15 minutes, and each response carries `meta.as_of`, the time of that refresh. Calls are rate limited per IP.\n\nFilters (all optional): `region` (comma-separated Region P-codes, e.g. ET04), `service_category` or `category`, `from` / `to` (YYYY-MM-DD), `month` (YYYY-MM), `granularity` (`month` or `week`). An unknown value is a 400 naming the field.\n\nThe admin endpoint (GET /api/v1/charts?charts=..., Grievance Admin) is not part of this collection. See docs/dashboard-analytics.md.\n\nAuth: public today. Once the Kong gateway enforces authorization, the charts need the OAN dashboards' API key (consumer `oan-dashboards`) in the `apikey` header: set `dashboard_api_key` in your own environment (current value only) and the collection sends it.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Sent only when set: public routes ignore it, the gateway needs it once it enforces keys.",
          "const key = pm.variables.get('dashboard_api_key');",
          "if (key) pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'apikey', value: key });"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// A request whose name ends in '→ NNN' expects that status; every other one is a public chart.",
          "const expected = pm.info.requestName.match(/→ (\\d{3})$/);",
          "if (expected) {",
          "    pm.test(`HTTP ${expected[1]}`, () => pm.response.to.have.status(Number(expected[1])));",
          "} else {",
          "    pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
          "    const body = pm.response.json();",
          "    pm.test('success envelope with rows', () => {",
          "        pm.expect(body.status).to.equal('success');",
          "        pm.expect(body.data).to.be.an('array');",
          "    });",
          "    pm.test('as_of is set (the rollup has run)', () => pm.expect(body.meta && body.meta.as_of).to.be.a('string'));",
          "    pm.test('no case detail in a public chart', () => {",
          "        const text = JSON.stringify(body.data);",
          "        ['ticket_number', 'title', 'submitter_display', 'description', 'assigned_dept'].forEach(k => pm.expect(text).to.not.include(`\"${k}\"`));",
          "    });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. KPIs: total, awaiting action, resolved, escalated",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/charts/grvKpis",
        "description": "Total with % change since the end of last month; Awaiting Action (Submitted + Assigned + In Progress) with new this week; Resolved (Resolved + Closed) with resolved this week; open escalated cases."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Performance KPIs (this month)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/charts/grvPerformanceKpis",
        "description": "Average resolution time (days), resolution rate, escalation rate and farmer satisfaction, each with its change against the previous month. A value is null when its denominator is zero."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Performance KPIs for a given month",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/charts/grvPerformanceKpis?month={{grievance_month}}"
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Monthly submission & resolution trend",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/charts/grvMonthlyTrend",
        "description": "Six months by default; months with nothing filed are zeros."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Weekly submission & resolution trend",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/charts/grvWeeklyTrend",
        "description": "Seven ISO weeks (Monday start) by default."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Net backlog trend (monthly)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
